    note: "*I'd rather* is very common in American conversation; *I'd prefer* sounds a little more careful. When ordering, Americans say *I'd like…*, *Could I have…?* or, very often, *Can I get…?*: *Can I get a coffee, please?* is everyday American usage, not rude.",
